  "headline": "Polda NTT Investigation Into Kupang Regent Rape Allegations Continues",
  "seoTitle": "Kupang Regent Rape Case Investigation Updates",
  "metaDescription": "Police in East Nusa Tenggara continue investigating rape allegations against the Kupang Regent as the Human Rights Minister calls for a swift resolution.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "Police in East Nusa Tenggara have received forensic results regarding the alleged sexual assault involving the Kupang Regent.",
    "The Regent has requested a delay in his scheduled questioning until Saturday, while investigators continue to interview relevant witnesses.",
    "Minister of Human Rights Natalius Pigai has engaged with the victim's family and requested that the regional police prioritize the case."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The East Nusa Tenggara Regional Police (Polda NTT) are currently investigating allegations of sexual assault involving the Regent of Kupang, Yosef Lede. Authorities confirmed they are in possession of the victim's forensic examination results and have begun gathering evidence, including personal items from the alleged victim. The investigation has drawn the attention of the Minister of Human Rights, Natalius Pigai, who has held meetings with the victim's family and publicly urged law enforcement to expedite the legal process. While police have called the Regent for questioning, the official requested a postponement of his examination until Saturday. Local authorities, including the regional Governor, have expressed support for an impartial investigation. The police have also interviewed additional witnesses, including members of the public order agency (Satpol PP), as part of the ongoing inquiry into the incident.",
